  "final_span": "the table with a toffee hammer.\nAfter 33 minutes had passed, Montreal gained a corner kick. The large 6-7 Drogba maneuvered to the forefront to powerfully header the ball backfield. Bernier, though small in build, found himself on the floor and managed to stand up using just one leg. The tiny crowd burst into delight.\nBernier struck the ball powerfully with two more hard headers as Montreal intensified their attack. He reached the second with mere moments left before halftime.\n\"Our pattern of play changed a little bit,\" Biello conceded. \"I don't know if I instructed guys to go away from the centre, but guys on the bench went away from the centre so right before the whistle Bernier was kind of isolated out front\u2026 We made a change right before the whistle hoping somebody would slide away from the centre.\"\nCheering diffused the goal, but",
